WEBVTT

00:00:00.00 --> 00:00:04.32
In the year 1279, the Song and Yuan armies fought their final decisive battle at Yamen.

00:00:04.32 --> 00:00:08.32
The Song army lashed more than a thousand warships together, resolved to fight with the sea at their backs.

00:00:08.32 --> 00:00:13.48
Warships crowded the sea, thick smoke hid the sun, and the war drums shook the sky.

00:00:13.48 --> 00:00:17.12
The two sides fought from dawn to dusk, with no clear winner.

00:00:17.12 --> 00:00:20.72
The Song army was defeated. Lu Xiufu carried the little emperor on his back and walked toward the sea.

00:00:20.72 --> 00:00:23.80
The little emperor was only eight years old, clinging tightly to Lu Xiufu.

00:00:23.80 --> 00:00:27.84
Holding his young sovereign, Lu Xiufu threw himself into the waves and died heroically for his country.

00:00:27.84 --> 00:00:31.48
Seeing this, the officers and soldiers beside him followed him in death, one after another.

00:00:31.48 --> 00:00:35.72
Beneath the setting sun, the Song army's banners slowly sank into the sea.

00:00:35.72 --> 00:00:39.96
A hundred thousand Southern Song soldiers and civilians sank to the seabed together with the great Song.

00:00:39.96 --> 00:00:42.24
When daylight came, the sea had grown calm again.

00:00:42.24 --> 00:00:45.68
The history of the Southern Song came to an end. After Yamen,

00:00:45.68 --> 00:00:49.04
there was no more Song dynasty, and China entered the Yuan era.
